         (src/remark-composer.js) needs a translation block to select text
         inside of, and the Remarks field to write the quote into. Right-
         click it -> Copy > Outer HTML (or `copy(el.outerHTML)` in the
         Console). See tests/fixtures/README.md for the full capture
         methodology.
      3. Scrub the translation text and any remark/reviewer content —
         replace with placeholder text of similar length and shape, keep
         structure/classes/data-* attributes real.
      4. Paste the scrubbed markup into <body> below, in place of the
         placeholder comment.
      5. Rename this file to quoting-bug-repro.html (drop the .template
         suffix) and open it in Firefox.
      6. Select text inside a translation block, press Q, and reproduce the
         bug. src/remark-composer.js's tryQuoteSelection() already documents
         three known, unfixed defects inline (unescaped `"` in the quoted
         text, no duplicate-quote guard, raw newlines kept in multi-line
         quotes) — check whether the bug you're chasing is one of those
         before assuming it's something new.
    -->
